{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_1", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For acid reflux, focusing on low-acid, high-fiber, and lean foods can help manage symptoms.\n\nRecommended foods include:\n*   **Fruits:** Bananas, melons (watermelon, cantaloupe, honeydew), apples, and pears are good low-acid choices. Berries can be consumed in moderation.\n*   **Vegetables:** Most green vegetables like spinach, broccoli, cabbage, carrots, green beans, peas, celery, and lettuce are beneficial. Sweet potatoes and baked potatoes are also good.\n*   **Whole Grains:** Oatmeal, brown rice, and whole-grain breads are excellent sources of fiber that can help absorb stomach acid. Other good options include quinoa, barley, and couscous.\n*   **Lean Proteins:** Opt for lean meats such as skinless chicken breast, fish, turkey, lean ground beef, and egg whites. Tofu is also a good protein source.\n*   **Dairy:** Choose low-fat or fat-free dairy products like yogurt, feta or goat cheese, and plant-based milks.\n*   **Nuts and Seeds:** Almonds, chia seeds, pumpkin seeds, flax seeds, sesame seeds, and sunflower seeds can be included.\n*   **Other helpful foods:** Ginger and fennel are known to calm the stomach. Vegetable broth and plenty of water are also recommended.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0042-37-07571:2": 0.9990792274475098, "clueweb22-en0018-80-17587:11": 0.9975409507751465, "clueweb22-en0005-41-09262:15": 0.9973226189613342, "clueweb22-en0023-31-01763:3": 0.9969127178192139, "clueweb22-en0002-93-16983:2": 0.996839165687561, "clueweb22-en0018-87-10874:14": 0.9964589476585388, "clueweb22-en0027-11-19840:5": 0.9961495399475098, "clueweb22-en0038-83-05173:5": 0.9960013031959534, "clueweb22-en0002-93-16983:1": 0.9959968328475952, "clueweb22-en0033-35-06828:4": 0.9956054091453552}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0042-37-07571:2": 0.9990792274475098, "clueweb22-en0004-73-09989:16": 0.9988