{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For stomach acid reflux, focusing on alkaline, low-fat, and high-fiber foods can be beneficial.\n\nGood options include:\n*   **Fruits:** Bananas and melons (like watermelon, cantaloupe, and honeydew) are highly alkaline and can help soothe the esophageal lining.\n*   **Vegetables:** Green vegetables such as asparagus, broccoli, spinach, kale, lettuce, celery, and carrots are low in fat and sugar, promoting better digestion. Root vegetables like sweet potatoes are also good.\n*   **Grains:** Oatmeal, brown rice, and other whole grains like quinoa and couscous are high in fiber, which can absorb stomach acid and reduce symptoms. Whole grain breads are also beneficial.\n*   **Lean Proteins:** Chicken, turkey, fish, seafood, tofu, and egg whites are good choices as they are low in fat and easier to digest.\n*   **Other helpful foods:** Ginger can help calm the stomach, and plain yogurt (especially fat-free) can also be soothing. Saltine crackers and vegetable broth can also provide relief.\n\nRemember to avoid high-fat, fried, and acidic foods, as well as spicy items, garlic, onions, and citrus fruits.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0009-09-00824:3": 0.996729850769043, "clueweb22-en0024-83-01996:17": 0.9962060451507568, "clueweb22-en0018-87-10874:14": 0.9956934452056885, "clueweb22-en0044-17-08661:4": 0.995649516582489, "clueweb22-en0005-41-09262:15": 0.9954633116722107, "clueweb22-en0027-01-14647:3": 0.9946610331535339, "clueweb22-en0044-72-05971:1": 0.9931600093841553, "clueweb22-en0032-91-00840:6": 0.9930360913276672, "clueweb22-en0002-93-16983:2": 0.9929976463317871, "clueweb22-en0000-61-09646:7": 0.9922682642936707, "clueweb22-en0018-80-17587:11": 0.9922232031822205, "clueweb22-en0011-63-17217:7": 0.9922009110450745, "clueweb22-en0018-80-17587:9": 0.9918859004974365, "clueweb22-en0039-15-05920:14": 0.9918553829193115