{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_4", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Here are some other foods you should generally avoid to help manage acid reflux:\n\n*   **High-Fat and Fried Foods:** This includes fried chicken, fatty cuts of meat (like marbled beef or bacon), fast food, high-fat salad dressings, creamy sauces, and high-fat pastries. These can relax the lower esophageal sphincter and slow digestion.\n*   **Acidic Foods:** Steer clear of tomatoes and tomato-based products (marinara sauce, ketchup, tomato soup), citrus fruits (lemons, oranges, grapefruit, cranberries), pineapple, and papaya.\n*   **Certain Beverages:** Avoid coffee, most teas (especially caffeinated ones), carbonated drinks (soda), alcohol (wine, liquor), and most fruit juices.\n*   **Spicy Foods:** Hot spices like chili and pepper flakes can irritate the esophagus.\n*   **Mint:** Peppermint and spearmint (including gum) are known triggers.\n*   **Chocolate:** It contains caffeine, fat, and cocoa, all of which can worsen reflux.\n*   **Onions and Garlic:** Especially raw onions, can be problematic for some.\n*   **High-Fat Dairy:** Full-fat milk, cheese, and sour cream might trigger symptoms.\n*   **Sugary Foods:** Candy, cake, desserts, and ice cream can also be problematic.\n*   **Eating Habits:** Additionally, try to avoid eating anything within two hours of going to bed.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-35-06828:4": 0.9987965822219849, "clueweb22-en0018-80-17587:9": 0.9985631108283997, "clueweb22-en0018-50-11252:14": 0.9985264539718628, "clueweb22-en0018-87-10874:12": 0.9984791874885559, "clueweb22-en0018-80-17587:10": 0.99836665391922, "clueweb22-en0032-91-00840:6": 0.9981909394264221, "clueweb22-en0018-87-10874:13": 0.9980878233909607, "clueweb22-en0015-25-04959:8": 0.998016357421875, "clueweb22-en0032-91-00840:7": 0.9978626370429993, "clueweb22-en0018-50-11252:15": 0.9977436065673828, "clueweb22-en0012-00-06