{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To help manage your acid reflux, especially considering your late dinner habit, recent weight gain, and desire for a lifestyle change, here are several suggestions:\n\nFirstly, regarding your late dinners, it's crucial to **avoid eating for at least three hours before lying down or going to bed**. This allows your stomach to digest food properly and minimizes acid reflux. Staying upright after meals can also help.\n\nFor weight management, **maintaining a healthy body weight** is highly recommended, as acid reflux is more prevalent in those who are overweight. **Regular exercise** and adopting a **healthier diet** focused on whole foods, low in fat and sugar, can support this.\n\nMore broadly, consider these lifestyle adjustments:\n*   **Eat smaller, more frequent meals** instead of large ones, and **eat slowly, chewing your food thoroughly**.\n*   **Avoid overeating**, as stomach distention can trigger reflux.\n*   **Limit or avoid trigger foods** like fatty, fried, spicy foods, chocolate, mint, carbonated drinks, alcohol, and caffeine.\n*   **Manage stress** through techniques like meditation or deep breathing, and ensure you get **enough sleep**.\n*   If you smoke, **quitting** can significantly reduce symptoms.\n\nThese changes can collectively help you manage acid reflux and contribute to your overall lifestyle goals.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0027-58-19039:6": 0.9424898028373718, "clueweb22-en0037-74-14945:10": 0.8731949925422668, "clueweb22-en0039-92-15038:12": 0.8649526238441467, "clueweb22-en0021-74-19197:6": 0.8584749102592468, "clueweb22-en0002-38-10912:5": 0.8583984375, "clueweb22-en0028-64-19668:2": 0.8458192944526672, "clueweb22-en0046-54-03909:9": 0.8173685073852539, "clueweb22-en0026-96-04891:1": 0.8165855407714844, "clueweb22-en0045-95-01180:2": 0.8094860315322876, "clueweb22-en0009-95-06055:9": 0