{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Apple cider vinegar can worsen acid reflux for some individuals, primarily because acid reflux isn't always caused by a lack of stomach acid. If your acid reflux is due to your digestive system producing *too much* digestive acid, then adding more acid through apple cider vinegar will only exacerbate the problem and make symptoms worse.\n\nFurthermore, the acidic nature of apple cider vinegar can directly irritate an already inflamed or aggravated stomach and esophagus, leading to more severe heartburn and discomfort. For those with silent reflux (LPR), acidic substances like apple cider vinegar can activate previously refluxed pepsin in the throat and airways, which then boosts its damaging potential and causes increased irritation of the mucous membranes. Therefore, it's important to understand the underlying cause of your acid reflux before using apple cider vinegar as a remedy.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0021-32-06040:5": 0.9060553908348083, "clueweb22-en0002-87-15707:6": 0.9056496620178223, "clueweb22-en0002-03-19296:5": 0.8994325399398804, "clueweb22-en0027-96-01816:1": 0.8992201685905457, "clueweb22-en0021-32-06040:4": 0.8959634900093079, "clueweb22-en0002-03-19296:6": 0.8894177079200745, "clueweb22-en0001-62-08246:7": 0.8870383501052856}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0023-70-15463:6": 0.9628283381462097, "clueweb22-en0030-73-19245:3": 0.9622957110404968, "clueweb22-en0038-17-12281:10": 0.9531525373458862, "clueweb22-en0030-73-19245:2": 0.9384775757789612, "clueweb22-en0012-37-01315:3": 0.9336062669754028, "clueweb22-en0042-89-04330:9": 0.9151849150657654, "clueweb22-en0001-07-10175:7": 0.9117904305458069, "clueweb22-en0021-32-06040:5": 0.9060553908348083, "clueweb22-en0002-87-15707:6": 0.9056496620178223, "clueweb22-en0007-10-18426:18": 0.9022263884544373, "clueweb22-en0002-03-19296: