{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Yes, stress, such as from an approaching deadline, can indeed worsen acid reflux symptoms.\n\nRegarding over-the-counter (OTC) medications for acid reflux, there are several types available:\n\n*   **Antacids**: These provide quick, short-term relief by neutralizing stomach acid. Examples include Tums, Rolaids, Mylanta, Maalox, Gaviscon, and Alka-Seltzer.\n*   **H2-receptor blockers (H2 blockers)**: These reduce acid production and offer longer relief than antacids. Common OTC examples are Cimetidine (Tagamet HB), Famotidine (Pepcid AC), Nizatidine (Axid AR), and Ranitidine (Zantac).\n*   **Proton Pump Inhibitors (PPIs)**: These are stronger medications that block acid production and can help heal the esophagus. OTC PPIs include Omeprazole (Prilosec OTC), Esomeprazole (Nexium 24HR), and Lansoprazole (Prevacid 24HR).\n*   **Alginates**: These work by forming a protective gel layer that floats on top of stomach acid, preventing it from rising into the esophagus. Gaviscon is an example of an alginate-containing medication.\n\nIt's generally recommended to try OTC options first. If your symptoms persist or worsen, it's best to consult a doctor.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0002-04-09789:3": 0.994526207447052, "clueweb22-en0017-96-03792:10": 0.9614062309265137, "clueweb22-en0011-58-02538:3": 0.9444946050643921, "clueweb22-en0039-92-15038:12": 0.9432330131530762, "clueweb22-en0016-97-03528:3": 0.9323940873146057, "clueweb22-en0019-30-04613:4": 0.9315044283866882, "clueweb22-en0006-20-05889:3": 0.9246161580085754, "clueweb22-en0006-20-05889:2": 0.9228684902191162, "clueweb22-en0015-45-13434:4": 0.9213970899581909, "clueweb22-en0019-41-03380:10": 0.9187396168708801, "clueweb22-en0016-90-04675:2": 0.917446494102478, "clueweb22-en0026-80-18810:6": 0.9163756370544434, "clueweb22-en0007-59-04070:8": 0.9139846563339233, "clueweb2