{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-2_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Sauvignon Blanc is renowned for its distinctive and easily identifiable taste, characterized by crisp, high acidity, often described as tangy, tart, or zesty, similar to a green apple. This acidity contributes to a refreshing and lively mouthfeel.\n\nA hallmark of Sauvignon Blanc is its herbaceous or \"green\" notes, primarily due to a compound called pyrazine. These notes can manifest as flavors and aromas of freshly cut grass, green bell pepper, and various herbs like basil, lemongrass, or nettles.\n\nThe specific taste profile is significantly influenced by the climate where the grapes are grown. In cooler climates, the wine typically exhibits more pronounced herbaceous and green characteristics, alongside citrus notes such as lime and grapefruit, and sometimes mineral undertones like flint or wet stone. In contrast, wines from warmer climates tend to develop riper, more tropical fruit flavors, including passion fruit, kiwi, honeydew melon, or peach, though they might lose some of the intense herbaceous aromas.\n\nWhile generally a dry white wine consumed young to preserve its bright acidity, some variations can exist based on winemaking techniques, potentially introducing subtle smokiness or, less commonly, notes of vanilla if oak-aged.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0035-41-12892:1": 0.9845715761184692, "clueweb22-en0028-55-10550:14": 0.9810256361961365, "clueweb22-en0045-11-17137:9": 0.9684138298034668, "clueweb22-en0028-55-10550:13": 0.959903359413147, "clueweb22-en0028-55-10550:11": 0.9387915134429932, "clueweb22-en0002-60-06769:10": 0.935759961605072, "clueweb22-en0020-01-13987:3": 0.9321628212928772, "clueweb22-en0004-10-03235:3": 0.9296353459358215, "clueweb22-en0010-68-13238:7": 0.9287576675415039, "clueweb22-en0021-40-10659:0": 0.9049304723739624, "clueweb22-en0042-39-10706:2": 0.8972166776657104, "clueweb