{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-2_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "It's a great idea to combine yoga with swimming for your recovery! London offers several excellent water spots, ranging from wild swimming locations to more traditional pools.\n\nFor open-water swimming, you could consider the **Hampstead Heath Bathing Ponds**, which are famed open-air swimming lakes with mixed, ladies', and men's ponds. Another popular choice is **Beckenham Place Park Swimming Lake**, a beautifully restored man-made lake, though it can be chilly and requires an induction and tow float. The **West Reservoir Centre in Hackney** is also a great open-water spot, managed by Better Leisure, and offers hot showers after your swim, though a wetsuit is mandatory.\n\nIf you're looking for a more controlled environment, especially given your past concern about cold water, a traditional pool or lido might be more comfortable. For instance, **Balham Leisure Centre** offers a modern 25-meter pool, perfect for lengths, and also has a steam room and sauna which could be beneficial for recovery. While the iconic **Serpentine Lido** in Hyde Park is popular, it's currently only open to existing members.\n\nRemember to check current opening times and booking requirements before visiting any of these locations.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0035-14-10039:0": 0.907230794429779, "clueweb22-en0036-25-05551:10": 0.7707194685935974, "clueweb22-en0023-06-14225:1": 0.7615818977355957, "clueweb22-en0044-22-03432:1": 0.737524688243866, "clueweb22-en0029-07-14670:0": 0.7367281913757324, "clueweb22-en0012-69-04768:3": 0.7319114208221436, "clueweb22-en0012-69-04768:0": 0.7159864902496338, "clueweb22-en0011-32-16579:10": 0.7021613717079163, "clueweb22-en0017-19-07439:0": 0.688783586025238, "clueweb22-en0042-14-10555:14": 0.6832854151725769, "clueweb22-en0035-14-10039:2": 0.6788569092750549, "clueweb22-en0025-02-05902:5": 0.6609959006