{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-2_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For your trip to New York, here are some general tips and suggestions for places to visit.\n\n**Travel Tips:**\n*   **Transportation:** The NYC Subway is an easy way to get around. Consider purchasing a seven-day unlimited pass for convenience. While you can rent a car for trips outside the city, the extensive subway and bus systems are excellent for navigating within the boroughs.\n*   **Explore Beyond Manhattan:** New York City has five diverse boroughs. Beyond Manhattan, explore Brooklyn for its fantastic food scene and brownstones, The Bronx for the Botanical Garden and Zoo, and Staten Island for great city views.\n*   **Save Money:** Look for free attractions like strolling along the Hudson River or enjoying Central Park. Many museums also offer free admission days or deals, so check their policies.\n*   **Bag Policy:** Be aware that many museums, stadiums, and concert halls have specific bag policies; check these before your visit to ensure entry.\n*   **Tipping:** It's standard practice to tip around 20% at restaurants in New York.\n\n**Places to Visit:**\nNew York City is packed with iconic attractions. Must-see spots include Times Square, the Empire State Building (or Top of the Rock for observation decks), and taking a ferry to see the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island. Central Park is a vast urban oasis perfect for relaxation, walking, or visiting sights like Belvedere Castle or the Central Park Zoo. Explore world-class museums such as the Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met) and the Museum of Modern Art (MoMA). Don't miss walking across the Brooklyn Bridge for stunning skyline views, catching a Broadway show, or enjoying the diverse culinary scene, including Brooklyn's famous pizza.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0037-56-08579:5": 0.9619333148002625, "clueweb22-en0036-97-04646:1": 0.9594438076019287, "clue