{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "New York City has several places that reflect Spanish culture and history. A historically significant area is \"Little Spain,\" located primarily on West 14th Street in Manhattan. This neighborhood served as a social and cultural hub for Spanish immigrants from the late 19th century. Key landmarks here include the Spanish Benevolent Society and the Church of Our Lady of Guadalupe, which was the first parish in Manhattan to offer mass in both Latin and Spanish. You might also find remnants of past businesses like Casa Moneo, a former Spanish food and gift emporium.\n\nAnother area with a strong Spanish-speaking heritage is East Harlem, also known as \"El Barrio.\" While it's famously the heart of Puerto Rican culture, it remains a diverse Latino neighborhood.\n\nFor modern Spanish culture, consider visiting Mercado Little Spain at Hudson Yards, a concept space by Chef Jos\u00e9 Andr\u00e9s focusing on Spanish cuisine, or Boqueria, a Barcelona-style tapas bar in Midtown Manhattan. Additionally, El Museo del Barrio in Upper Manhattan is dedicated to Latin American culture, which includes a rich Spanish heritage.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0027-43-00301:29": 0.8252904415130615, "clueweb22-en0011-89-10290:8": 0.8153085112571716, "clueweb22-en0011-89-10290:9": 0.7638716101646423, "clueweb22-en0011-89-10290:4": 0.7259974479675293, "clueweb22-en0011-89-10290:0": 0.6805140376091003, "clueweb22-en0035-03-12701:2": 0.6501237750053406, "clueweb22-en0000-24-17120:0": 0.6409507393836975, "clueweb22-en0035-03-12701:1": 0.6208903789520264, "clueweb22-en0014-64-05304:3": 0.6043549180030823, "clueweb22-en0031-28-14810:5": 0.5222858190536499, "clueweb22-en0035-03-12701:5": 0.5111748576164246, "clueweb22-en0033-89-11446:4": 0.48928961157798767}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0041-07-14304:2": 0.8288252353668213,