{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-1_1", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To help you prepare healthier meals at home with more nutrients and protein, while also considering low-carb options and boosting your calcium intake, here are some ingredient suggestions:\n\nFor **protein and nutrients**, incorporate lean meats like chicken, turkey, or fish such as salmon and tuna. Eggs are excellent and versatile. Plant-based protein sources like beans, peas, lentils, tofu, nuts, and seeds are highly nutritious. Brown rice offers more fiber and nutrients than white rice. Include a variety of colorful vegetables like spinach, kale, broccoli, and peppers for vitamins and antioxidants.\n\nFor **low-carb options**, Greek yogurt is a great choice, also being high in protein. Salmon, other fatty fish, and grilled plain chicken breast are excellent low-carb protein sources. Eggs are another fantastic low-carb meal option, especially when paired with spinach. Low-fat cheese can also be a carb-free protein source.\n\nTo boost your **calcium intake**, dairy products like Greek yogurt, low-fat milk, and cheese are excellent sources, many also being high in protein. If you prefer dairy alternatives, look for unsweetened, calcium-fortified soy, almond, or rice milk. Green leafy vegetables such as kale, spinach, and broccoli also provide calcium. Additionally, foods rich in vitamin B6, like lean meats, fish, and legumes, can help with calcium absorption.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0011-15-12952:8": 0.9397030472755432, "clueweb22-en0042-94-08603:4": 0.9331194758415222, "clueweb22-en0030-46-01532:4": 0.924668550491333, "clueweb22-en0019-11-06151:3": 0.9153204560279846, "clueweb22-en0045-45-05366:5": 0.8868988752365112, "clueweb22-en0001-57-19239:2": 0.881502628326416, "clueweb22-en0029-34-01073:4": 0.8784757256507874, "clueweb22-en0019-11-06151:2": 0.8760087490081787, "clueweb22-en0042-75-17311:5": 0.87543398141