{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To start your day with healthy and nutritious ingredients, focus on incorporating protein, fiber, and healthy fats.\n\nFor protein, consider eggs (scrambled, omelets with vegetables like spinach, peppers, or mushrooms), low-fat yogurt (plain or Greek), cottage cheese, or a scoop of protein powder in smoothies. Nuts and seeds like almonds, walnuts, chia seeds, and flax seeds are also excellent protein sources and can be added to oatmeal or yogurt. For calcium, milk and yogurt are great options.\n\nInstead of white bread, opt for whole-grain alternatives like whole-wheat toast, pita, or English muffins. For cereals, choose minimally processed whole-grain options like rolled oats or steel-cut oats, which are also good sources of fiber and protein.\n\nTo cut down on carbs and add nutrients, smoothies are a great choice. Blend low-carb ingredients like almond milk, keto yogurt, protein powder, and berries, or add greens like spinach and kale.\n\nWhen it comes to toppings and condiments, swap sugary jams and jellies for fresh or frozen fruits like berries or sliced apples. Be mindful of sugary drinks and choose water, unsweetened coffee, or tea instead.\n\nBy focusing on these nutrient-dense ingredients, you can build a healthier and more satisfying breakfast.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0000-22-04909:1": 0.9610475301742554, "clueweb22-en0040-10-14443:7": 0.9536519050598145, "clueweb22-en0028-96-01184:4": 0.9398961663246155, "clueweb22-en0031-28-15273:9": 0.9338162541389465, "clueweb22-en0016-81-12880:12": 0.915862500667572, "clueweb22-en0022-86-04257:1": 0.9151563048362732, "clueweb22-en0016-81-12880:13": 0.8999514579772949}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0000-22-04909:1": 0.9610475301742554, "clueweb22-en0023-06-03871:6": 0.9559645652770996, "clueweb22-en0040-10-14443:7": 0.9536519050598145, "clue