{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Beyond the rice alternatives we discussed, there are many other low-carb and high-nutrient options for your lunch.\n\nFor pasta, consider **courgetti** (zucchini noodles) or carrot and courgette noodles, which can be used in dishes like Zucchini Pad Thai. If you usually have sandwiches, **lettuce wraps** are an excellent low-carb substitute for bread, allowing you to wrap lean meats like turkey or chicken, cheese, and vegetables.\n\nInstead of potatoes, you can try **mashed carrots**, **mashed rutabaga**, or **celery root**, which are lower in carbs and offer different nutrient profiles.\n\nYou can also build your lunch around protein-rich salads. Options include **tuna and avocado salad**, **Caprese salad with cauliflower**, **Tuna and Egg Salad**, or **Steak Salad**. Incorporating ingredients like **tofu** or **tempeh** offers high-protein, low-carb plant-based options.\n\nMany vegetables are naturally low-carb and nutrient-dense, forming a great base for your meals. Think spinach, lettuce, avocado, asparagus, cucumbers, tomatoes, zucchini, broccoli, green beans, and peppers. These can be steamed, roasted, or added fresh to salads, providing essential vitamins and fiber.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0002-97-02341:4": 0.9256614446640015, "clueweb22-en0041-75-00542:5": 0.9153912663459778, "clueweb22-en0038-86-16888:20": 0.8770579099655151, "clueweb22-en0024-25-19291:1": 0.832197904586792, "clueweb22-en0022-48-17466:1": 0.8057959079742432, "clueweb22-en0041-75-00542:4": 0.7863725423812866, "clueweb22-en0037-64-10515:14": 0.7830278873443604, "clueweb22-en0022-48-17466:5": 0.782914936542511, "clueweb22-en0015-58-07396:3": 0.7729201912879944, "clueweb22-en0003-79-04263:2": 0.771542489528656}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0002-97-02341:4": 0.9256614446640015, "clueweb22-en0041-75-00542:5": 0.915391