{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_4", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Yes, you will need to make some important changes to your diet during pregnancy to support both your health and your baby's development.\n\nFocus on a healthy, balanced, and varied diet rich in nutrient-dense, whole foods. While you don't need to \"eat for two,\" your calorie needs will increase in the second and third trimesters.\n\nKey dietary recommendations include:\n*   **Emphasize:** Plenty of fruits and vegetables (aim for at least 5 portions daily), whole grains (like whole wheat bread and brown rice instead of white varieties), lean proteins, and calcium-rich foods.\n*   **Nutrients:** Ensure adequate intake of calcium (1000-1300 mg daily from sources like dairy, baked potatoes, navy beans), iron (27 mg daily from lean meats, spinach, beans), and iodine (220 mcg daily).\n*   **Supplements:** It's highly recommended to take a prenatal vitamin daily, which typically includes folic acid (essential until week 12) and vitamin D, among other vital nutrients. Discuss the right product with your doctor.\n*   **Hydration:** Drink plenty of water, aiming for about 10 cups (2 liters) daily.\n\nYou should also limit or avoid certain foods:\n*   **Sugary foods and drinks:** Reduce intake of cakes, biscuits, and sodas, as they offer low nutritional value and high sugar content.\n*   **Carbohydrate-restrictive diets:** Avoid diets like keto or Atkins, as your growing baby needs carbohydrates, and ketosis can be harmful.\n*   **Raw or undercooked foods:** Steer clear of raw meat, eggs, seafood, and unpasteurized dairy products or juices due to the risk of harmful bacteria.\n*   **High-mercury fish:** Avoid shark, swordfish, and marlin, and limit other oily fish.\n*   **High-salt foods:** Reduce cured meats, some sauces, and salted nuts.\n\nEating small, regular meals can also help manage common pregnancy symptoms like nausea. Always consult your doctor or a dietitian for personalized dietary advice.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0008-41-08982:10": 0.9768721461296082, "clueweb22-en0010-45-05047:1": 0.9741429686546326, "clueweb22-en0018-28-09879:1": 0.9701356887817383, "clueweb22-en0027-79-08948:2": 0.9700286388397217, "clueweb22-en0044-57-08176:5": 0.967968225479126, "clueweb22-en0008-96-17009:5": 0.9675169587135315, "clueweb22-en0008-96-17009:6": 0.9646791815757751, "clueweb22-en0012-00-00714:1": 0.9634288549423218, "clueweb22-en0001-10-19534:7": 0.963361918926239, "clueweb22-en0026-42-08361:1": 0.9624053239822388, "clueweb22-en0023-20-17679:9": 0.9605302810668945, "clueweb22-en0037-54-02698:9": 0.9578269124031067, "clueweb22-en0016-91-07792:7": 0.9555076360702515, "clueweb22-en0005-62-04180:12": 0.9548226594924927, "clueweb22-en0038-78-08235:8": 0.9547268152236938, "clueweb22-en0006-84-04674:7": 0.9546544551849365, "clueweb22-en0038-42-08150:10": 0.9542111754417419, "clueweb22-en0018-98-03628:11": 0.9538604021072388, "clueweb22-en0016-34-04507:4": 0.9526754021644592}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0008-41-08982:10": 0.9768721461296082, "clueweb22-en0010-45-05047:1": 0.9741429686546326, "clueweb22-en0018-28-09879:1": 0.9701356887817383, "clueweb22-en0027-79-08948:2": 0.9700286388397217, "clueweb22-en0044-57-08176:5": 0.967968225479126, "clueweb22-en0008-96-17009:5": 0.9675169587135315, "clueweb22-en0008-96-17009:6": 0.9646791815757751, "clueweb22-en0012-00-00714:1": 0.9634288549423218, "clueweb22-en0001-10-19534:7": 0.963361918926239, "clueweb22-en0026-42-08361:1": 0.9624053239822388, "clueweb22-en0023-20-17679:9": 0.9605302810668945, "clueweb22-en0017-18-15335:13": 0.960407555103302, "clueweb22-en0037-54-02698:9": 0.9578269124031067, "clueweb22-en0016-91-07792:7": 0.9555076360702515, "clueweb22-en0005-62-04180:12": 0.9548226594924927, "clueweb22-en0038-78-08235:8": 0.9547268152236938, "clueweb22-en0006-84-04674:7": 0.9546544551849365, "clueweb22-en0038-42-08150: