{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Both microdermabrasion and chemical peels have potential side effects.\n\nFor **microdermabrasion**, side effects are generally mild, including slight irritation, redness, swelling, or a sunburned sensation for a few days. You might also experience mild inflammation or flaky skin. Rarely, it can lead to infection, bruising, pinpoint bleeding, or even skin damage like lesions and scratches if performed aggressively. There's also a risk of reactivating dormant viruses like herpes.\n\n**Chemical peels** have a wider range of potential side effects depending on their depth. Common effects include redness, swelling, flaking, and a burning or stinging sensation. Your skin will also be highly sensitive to sunlight for several days or weeks. Deeper peels carry more significant risks such as infection, scarring, blistering, throbbing, and temporary or permanent skin discoloration, including demarcation lines between treated and untreated areas. In rare cases, especially with very deep peels, more severe systemic issues like heart, kidney, or liver damage, skin hypersensitivity, or cracking have been reported.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-06-10590:10": 0.8331257104873657, "clueweb22-en0033-06-10590:9": 0.7833353877067566, "clueweb22-en0036-14-13056:11": 0.771841824054718, "clueweb22-en0032-47-03490:7": 0.7225816249847412, "clueweb22-en0033-06-10590:7": 0.6468052268028259, "clueweb22-en0004-95-05610:11": 0.6405355930328369, "clueweb22-en0024-80-03963:1": 0.538635790348053, "clueweb22-en0033-06-10590:4": 0.5341910123825073, "clueweb22-en0023-28-09850:10": 0.5119616389274597, "clueweb22-en0037-85-14845:4": 0.48559877276420593}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-06-10590:10": 0.8331257104873657, "clueweb22-en0033-06-10590:9": 0.7833353877067566, "clueweb22-en0036-14-13056:11": 0.771841824054718, "cluew