{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "After microneedling, it's crucial to adjust your skincare routine to allow your skin to heal properly. While your current routine includes beneficial ingredients, some should be temporarily avoided.\n\nYou should **avoid** using Retinol, Vitamin C (especially high concentrations or low pH formulations), and AHA/BHA serums immediately after microneedling. These active ingredients can be irritating and potentially harmful to your sensitized skin. Most experts recommend waiting at least 5 to 7 days, or until any redness and irritation have subsided, before reintroducing them.\n\nHowever, your daily Hyaluronic Acid application is highly recommended. Hyaluronic acid is excellent for hydrating and supporting the skin's healing process after microneedling, and the procedure can optimize its absorption.\n\nFor the first few days, stick to gentle, non-irritating cleansers, and focus on keeping your skin hydrated with products like hyaluronic acid, ceramides, or peptides. Always apply a broad-spectrum, fragrance-free mineral sunscreen with at least SPF 30 when going outside, as your skin will be more sensitive to UV damage.\n\nRegarding your La Roche-Posay Vitamin C serum, it would fall under the recommendation to avoid Vitamin C immediately post-treatment. The provided passages do not contain information about specific product lines like La Roche-Posay in relation to nut allergies, so you should always check the ingredient list of any product you use to ensure it's safe for your allergy.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-70-02855:6": 0.703700065612793, "clueweb22-en0009-89-01915:5": 0.6814190745353699, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:2": 0.6133086085319519, "clueweb22-en0016-51-13074:5": 0.5826539993286133, "clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:10": 0.5698947310447693, "clueweb22-en0033-70-02855:5": 0.5566211938858032, "clueweb22-en0019-72-