{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "7-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Bread machines offer significant advantages for home baking, primarily convenience and control. They automate the entire process, from mixing and kneading to rising and baking, saving you considerable time and effort. Many models include a timer, allowing you to wake up to fresh bread or have it ready after work, and the process is generally mess-free.\n\nAnother major benefit is the ability to control ingredients, which is ideal for dietary needs like allergies or gluten sensitivities, and allows for customization with add-ins like nuts or fruits. Baking at home with a machine can also be more cost-effective in the long run compared to buying store-bought bread, and they are generally energy-efficient. You can make various types of bread, doughs for pizza or pasta, and even jam.\n\nHowever, there are some drawbacks. Bread machine loaves might have a denser texture, and the crust can be thicker and tougher than oven-baked bread. A common complaint is the hole left by the mixing blades at the bottom of the loaf. While highly convenient, they generally cannot produce authentic artisan sourdough loaves, and you're typically limited to baking one loaf at a time. Despite these minor cons, a bread machine is a great tool for consistent, fresh homemade bread with minimal effort.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0004-55-04669:15": 0.9443982243537903, "clueweb22-en0001-02-06498:15": 0.8487623929977417, "clueweb22-en0028-08-10427:9": 0.8468767404556274, "clueweb22-en0004-55-04669:16": 0.8063092827796936, "clueweb22-en0004-55-04669:17": 0.8015403747558594, "clueweb22-en0031-00-03222:8": 0.7703856825828552, "clueweb22-en0017-06-08603:7": 0.6867672801017761, "clueweb22-en0001-02-06498:14": 0.6853642463684082, "clueweb22-en0020-11-12654:2": 0.679191529750824, "clueweb22-en0001-76-10350:5": 0.6696977019309998, "clueweb22-en0010-60-0703