{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_1", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Managing ADHD in an office with a sedentary lifestyle involves a combination of strategies to address common symptoms.\n\nTo combat distractibility, consider requesting a quiet workspace or using noise-cancelling headphones or white noise. Maintain an organized, clutter-free desk, and try to focus on one task at a time, routing calls to voicemail to check at set times.\n\nFor hyperactivity in a sedentary role, incorporate frequent breaks to move around, like walking to the water cooler or mailroom. Use your lunch hour for exercise, and take notes during meetings to help with restlessness. Regular physical activity, such as a 15-minute power walk, can also help channel energy and improve focus.\n\nTo improve memory and organization, utilize notes, checklists, and digital reminders for deadlines. Avoid over-scheduling by practicing saying no to new tasks and breaking down large projects into smaller, manageable steps, perhaps using 15-minute focus blocks.\n\nIf impulsivity is a challenge, practice self-talk, relaxation techniques like deep breathing, and anticipate situations that trigger impulsive reactions. Seeking feedback or working with a coach can also be beneficial. Additionally, ensure you get enough sleep and engage in regular exercise, as these foundational habits significantly support ADHD management.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:4": 0.9764827489852905, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:5": 0.9740132093429565, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:8": 0.9644696712493896, "clueweb22-en0000-31-16466:2": 0.9524510502815247, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:10": 0.9470938444137573, "clueweb22-en0033-18-04361:18": 0.9424805045127869, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:3": 0.9387153387069702, "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:10": 0.9357384443283081, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:1": 0.9332865476608276, "clueweb22-en0009-70-10081:11": 0.9231