{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Feeling overwhelmed by a large number of tasks is a common challenge for adults with ADHD. Here are some strategies that can help you manage this at your office job:\n\nA key approach is to **break down large projects or tasks into smaller, more manageable steps**. Focus on completing one step at a time, and avoid starting new tasks until your current one is finished. This helps prevent feeling scattered and makes the workload less daunting.\n\nTo manage the overall volume, **simplify your schedule** by avoiding over-scheduling yourself. Practice saying no to new tasks if you know they will add undue stress or prevent you from focusing on current priorities.\n\nUtilize **organizational and time management tools** consistently. This could include a paper planner, digital apps like Trello or Todoist, or time-management methods like the Pomodoro Technique (working in focused intervals with breaks). Consider setting clear deadlines for yourself or asking your supervisor to help set them for tasks.\n\nWhen you complete a task or a significant step, **reward yourself**. This can be a small, enjoyable activity like a short walk or a favorite song, providing motivation to keep going. If you start to feel stressed or overwhelmed, take a short relaxation break to regain composure.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:8": 0.9890676140785217, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:9": 0.9667046666145325, "clueweb22-en0033-18-04361:4": 0.9629517793655396, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:3": 0.957146406173706, "clueweb22-en0031-34-14667:27": 0.9547634720802307, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:11": 0.954730749130249, "clueweb22-en0035-93-06191:20": 0.951127827167511, "clueweb22-en0040-44-04493:6": 0.9504533410072327, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:10": 0.9496362209320068, "clueweb22-en0022-96-02784:6": 0.9398600459098816, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:7"