{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Hyperfocus is a powerful state for productivity. To protect it from distractions like emails and meetings, a key strategy is to proactively manage your environment and schedule.\n\nBefore entering hyperfocus, turn off all non-essential notifications on your computer and phone, and consider putting your devices on \"do not disturb\" or airplane mode. Using noise-canceling headphones can also help create a focused environment.\n\nFor emails, avoid checking them constantly. Instead, pre-decide specific times to check your inbox, perhaps once or twice a day, and only when you have the time and energy to deal with them. You can even set an auto-responder for urgent requests, directing people to call you if it's truly critical.\n\nFor scheduled meetings, try to block out dedicated \"deep work\" time in your diary when you know you're most likely to hyperfocus, and schedule meetings around these periods, perhaps in the late afternoon. If you must attend a meeting, ensure it has a clear agenda to maximize efficiency and minimize the disruption to your flow.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0041-12-03522:5": 0.9103772044181824, "clueweb22-en0000-56-03635:8": 0.8235129117965698, "clueweb22-en0022-33-08001:9": 0.7399976253509521, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:1": 0.7381373643875122, "clueweb22-en0016-22-09673:7": 0.7211108803749084, "clueweb22-en0014-37-11521:3": 0.7107100486755371, "clueweb22-en0041-12-03522:7": 0.7075446248054504, "clueweb22-en0030-68-01581:10": 0.691075325012207}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:8": 0.9233013987541199, "clueweb22-en0041-12-03522:5": 0.9103772044181824, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:4": 0.8524991869926453, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:5": 0.8410987854003906, "clueweb22-en0000-56-03635:8": 0.8235129117965698, "clueweb22-en0012-71-04546:18": 0.7857927083969116, "clueweb22