{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To manage transitions before and after meetings and reset your focus, several strategies can be very helpful.\n\nBefore a meeting, you can create a buffer in your calendar by scheduling meetings for 25 or 50 minutes instead of the full 30 or 60. This gives you a few minutes to prepare mentally or wrap up a task without rushing. You could also take a quick 60-second time-out to reground yourself, perhaps by closing your eyes and taking a few deep breaths.\n\nAfter a meeting, it's crucial to pause before jumping into the next task. Take a micro-break by stepping away from your desk, shaking out your body, stretching, or resting your eyes. Even a short walk, especially for a sedentary office job, can help reset your mental energy. You can also use this time for a quick meditation to reboot your focus. Some people find it helpful to establish a \"transition ritual\" like putting on a specific playlist, pouring a fresh cup of tea, or doing a quick stretch to signal the shift back to focused work.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0023-69-08765:9": 0.8830143213272095, "clueweb22-en0006-00-08364:15": 0.6553508639335632, "clueweb22-en0006-00-08364:14": 0.6546827554702759, "clueweb22-en0021-80-10230:3": 0.5629675388336182, "clueweb22-en0017-46-05051:7": 0.5244156122207642, "clueweb22-en0031-74-07881:9": 0.4953168034553528, "clueweb22-en0022-70-00626:6": 0.47680360078811646, "clueweb22-en0004-26-01070:10": 0.4368616044521332, "clueweb22-en0030-09-09011:14": 0.41453954577445984}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0023-69-08765:9": 0.8830143213272095, "clueweb22-en0023-04-02960:4": 0.7880837917327881, "clueweb22-en0006-00-08364:15": 0.6553508639335632, "clueweb22-en0006-00-08364:14": 0.6546827554702759, "clueweb22-en0014-49-11632:7": 0.6124445199966431, "clueweb22-en0021-80-10230:3": 0.5629675388336182, "clueweb22