{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-2_3", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Beyond your tattoo machine and fake skin, here's a list of essential supplies for applying ink as a self-taught hobbyist, with a strong emphasis on safety and hygiene:\n\nYou'll need **tattoo ink** (consider starting with black and a few basic colors) and **sterile tattoo needles** in assorted sizes. To power your machine, acquire a **power supply, clip cord, and a foot pedal**.\n\nFor the actual application, get **tattoo grips** (disposable are often recommended for beginners), **ink cups** and an **ink cup holder**, along with small but crucial items like **grommets, O-rings, and rubber bands** for your machine setup.\n\n**Hygiene and safety are paramount**: Stock up on **disposable gloves** (nitrile or latex), a specialized **disinfectant** for surfaces, **antibacterial/green soap**, **skin cleansers**, and **antiseptic wipes**. You'll also need **sterile ointment** (like Vaseline or petroleum jelly), **bandages**, and **hospital tape** for fresh tattoos. A **sharps container** is essential for safe needle disposal. Consider **plastic cover sheets** for your workspace and machine to maintain cleanliness.\n\nFinally, for preparation and maintenance, you'll want **tattoo transfer paper** and a **marker pen** for designs, **cleaning brushes** for your equipment, and **adjustment tools**. Having some **aftercare products** (e.g., A&D ointment or specialized tattoo balm) is also wise. Numbing cream is optional for sensitive areas.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0001-91-13299:14": 0.48318567872047424, "clueweb22-en0020-24-16033:20": 0.44497716426849365, "clueweb22-en0020-24-16033:21": 0.4421866536140442, "clueweb22-en0032-43-06101:5": 0.40664908289909363, "clueweb22-en0030-49-10071:8": 0.39700058102607727, "clueweb22-en0001-91-13299:15": 0.3802591562271118, "clueweb22-en0014-92-17969:15": 0.31902366876602173, "clueweb22-e