{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For your mountain bike, used on forest trails and rough paths where comfort is key, you'll want a saddle designed to absorb bumps and provide ample cushioning.\n\nMountain bike saddles generally have more padding than narrow racing saddles to handle the rough terrain you'll encounter. Comfort saddles are typically wider and feature more padding, making them suitable for longer rides where comfort is essential. While cruiser saddles offer maximum cushioning, they are usually for short, leisurely rides and might not be efficient for your type of riding.\n\nLook for saddles with features like heavy foam cushioning, gel padding, or orthopedic comfort foam to maximize relief. Some advanced saddles, like the SQlab 611 Ergowave, are designed to flex with your pedaling motion for a more anatomical fit and improved efficiency.\n\nSpecific examples of comfortable mountain bike saddles include the Ergon SM Saddle and Selle Italia Diva Gel Superflow Saddle (especially for women), which are designed for various mountain biking styles like All-Mountain, Trail, and Cross-Country. The SPANK OOZY 220 is also noted for providing support on varied terrain. Remember that choosing the right saddle for your riding style and body shape is crucial to avoid discomfort and chafing.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0034-10-16829:4": 0.9050184488296509, "clueweb22-en0007-52-02129:8": 0.8929022550582886, "clueweb22-en0007-52-02129:10": 0.8651453256607056, "clueweb22-en0046-56-06798:11": 0.8624361157417297, "clueweb22-en0020-02-10977:12": 0.8585504293441772, "clueweb22-en0020-10-04236:16": 0.8583282828330994, "clueweb22-en0020-02-10977:11": 0.8372116684913635}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0034-10-16829:4": 0.9050184488296509, "clueweb22-en0034-15-13457:6": 0.90326327085495, "clueweb22-en0022-19-17552:3": 0.9007524847984314, "