{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Given your preference for the softness of gel seats, your past back pain, and your concern about slipping, there are several important features to consider for a gel cushion add-on.\n\nBeyond the anti-slip interior and straps you mentioned, look for cushions with **enhanced shock absorption**. This is crucial for your mountain biking on forest trails and rough paths, as it will significantly reduce discomfort from bumps and protect your lower back and sit bones.\n\nAnother vital feature for your back pain is a **pressure relief design**, such as a central cutout or a channel. These designs are engineered to alleviate pressure on sensitive areas and support a healthier posture, which can greatly improve comfort during rides.\n\nConsider **breathability** to prevent heat buildup, especially on longer rides, as some gel cushions are designed to dissipate heat effectively. Since you ride in rainy weather, a **waterproof cover** or a cushion made with weather-resistant material is also a practical feature to keep your seat dry and extend its life.\n\nWhile gel can compact over time, some cushions are designed with multiple layers or technologies to minimize this, offering **lasting comfort** and preventing the \"bottoming out\" feeling. Prioritizing these key features will help you find a comfortable and durable gel cushion that suits your riding style and addresses your concerns without overwhelming you with too many technical choices.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0013-27-14778:2": 0.8729325532913208, "clueweb22-en0040-31-08734:5": 0.8517688512802124, "clueweb22-en0013-65-08307:8": 0.8489813208580017, "clueweb22-en0032-13-00097:2": 0.848569393157959, "clueweb22-en0040-31-08734:6": 0.8442190289497375, "clueweb22-en0032-13-00097:4": 0.843985915184021, "clueweb22-en0002-29-09374:10": 0.8363088965415955, "clueweb22-en0027-38