{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The \"jockey\" you're referring to are the jockey wheels, also known as pulley wheels, which are crucial components of your bike's rear derailleur. There are two of them, housed within the derailleur's cage, typically guiding the chain in an S-shaped pattern.\n\nEach jockey wheel has a distinct function:\n*   **Upper Jockey Wheel (Guide Pulley):** This wheel is responsible for guiding the chain precisely onto the correct sprocket when you shift gears. It literally guides the chain in the direction it needs to go.\n*   **Lower Jockey Wheel (Tension Pulley):** This wheel's primary role is to maintain proper chain tension. As you shift between different gears (which have varying sizes), the lower jockey wheel takes up or releases chain slack, ensuring the chain remains taut and doesn't sag or jump off. This continuous tension is vital for smooth shifting and preventing the chain from derailing.\n\nTogether, these wheels work to facilitate gear changes and ensure consistent chain tension across all gear combinations.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:1": 0.8765608668327332, "clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:0": 0.8443006277084351, "clueweb22-en0022-23-00873:11": 0.7346370816230774, "clueweb22-en0026-74-04945:5": 0.5783487558364868, "clueweb22-en0018-20-12295:7": 0.5308892130851746, "clueweb22-en0018-20-12295:16": 0.47325217723846436}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:1": 0.8765608668327332, "clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:0": 0.8443006277084351, "clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:1": 0.749475359916687, "clueweb22-en0022-23-00873:11": 0.7346370816230774, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:2": 0.7150372266769409, "clueweb22-en0040-35-09091:5": 0.645959198474884, "clueweb22-en0019-65-12165:1": 0.6264308094978333, "clueweb22-en0022-23-00873:10": 0.5996873378753662, "clueweb22-en0026-74-04945:5": 0.578348755836